residual and the Jacobian for conditioning (see `_set_charge_row_scale`). This was
verified by inspection (grep for the 4 leftover-edit signatures from items 1-3: none
present; grep for `charge_row_scale`/`_set_charge_row_scale`: present, matching the
coordinator's description) -- not a leftover red-state edit of mine.

After rebuilding, all 19 tests in test/rmgpy/solver/plasmaWallTest.py still PASS
(`pytest test/rmgpy/solver/plasmaWallTest.py -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q`: "19
passed in 2.78s"). The one existing test that touches the electron residual row,
test_quasineutral_electron_row_is_net_charge_with_no_dydt_dependence, remains valid
unmodified: its state is charge-neutral by construction (net_charge == 0.0 exactly),
so `charge_row_scale * 0.0 == 0.0` regardless of the scale's value -- confirmed
empirically that charge_row_scale != 1.0 for that reactor (47024667.78...) while the
test still passes, i.e. the test was already scale-invariant and needed no edit.

