4. test_net_charge_flux_zero_on_neutral_nonzero_on_nonneutral
================================================================================

Edit (in _apply_wall_terms, the charged-species loss loop):

--- a/rmgpy/solver/plasma.pyx
+++ b/rmgpy/solver/plasma.pyx
@@ _apply_wall_terms
-            loss = nu * y[j]
+            loss = (nu * 1.01 if j == self.electron_index else nu) * y[j]

Rationale: gives the electron a slightly different wall loss frequency than the ions,
breaking the "one common ambipolar loss frequency for every charged species" design and
making the net charge flux to the wall on an initially-neutral state non-zero instead of
zero (an electron-preferential loss un-neutralises the plasma at the wall).

