15. test_charge_row_scale_is_positive_finite_and_leaves_the_solution_unchanged
================================================================================

Edit (in residual, the quasineutrality electron row):

--- a/rmgpy/solver/plasma.pyx
+++ b/rmgpy/solver/plasma.pyx
@@ residual
-            delta[self.electron_index] = self.charge_row_scale * self._net_charge(y)
+            delta[self.electron_index] = self.charge_row_scale * self.charge_row_scale * self._net_charge(y)

Rationale: squares the row-scale multiplier in the residual only (the Jacobian still applies it
to the first power at line ~1851), breaking the design invariant that charge_row_scale is an
EXACT row scaling of the DAE. This makes the analytic Jacobian inconsistent with the residual it
is supposed to linearise, so DASPK's Newton iteration on the algebraic electron row is no longer
consistent between the two reactors compared in the test (ra.charge_row_scale=1.0 vs
rb.charge_row_scale=1.0e6): the ra case is unaffected (1.0**2 == 1.0) but the rb case's residual
row is now scaled 1e6x relative to what its Jacobian predicts, driving the corrector to fail.

Failing pytest output (rebuilt .so, ran the single test node):

